---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url, issueUrl } from '../lib/site';

const formHref = issueUrl('submit-material.yml');
---

<Base title="Share a material" description="How to share a study material with the library.">
  <h1>Share a material</h1>
  <p class="lead">It takes about two minutes. A moderator reviews every submission before it appears.</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><strong>Check that you may share it.</strong> Read the <a href={url('/policy/')}>content policy</a>. Share only your own work, material the instructor allows, openly licensed material, or material the university permits.</li>
    <li><strong>Put the file somewhere it opens without logging in.</strong> For example, a Google Drive or OneDrive file set to “anyone with the link can view”.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Send the details.</strong>
      {formHref
        ? <a class="button" href={formHref}>Open the submission form</a>
        : <span>The form link appears here once the site is connected to its GitHub repository.</span>}
    </li>
    <li><strong>Wait for review.</strong> If it is accepted, it is added to the library. If not, you are told why.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="meta">The form needs a free GitHub account. A way to submit without one is planned.</p>
</Base>
